From ca31dc6e90556aaa7924031c9e3caf8154dc148c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Emmanuel=20Podest=C3=A1=20Junior?= <epodesta@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:11:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): #159 dual-accept Cognito strategy (dark by
 default)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirror of the back4-api dual-accept work (feat/cognito-dual-accept) for the
NestJS primary-api relying party, so the LEGACY packiot40 customer plane can
accept a Cognito ID token OR a Firebase token during the Firebase→Cognito
cutover (ADR-0034 / docs/plans/firebase-to-cognito-migration-epic.md).

- CognitoStrategy: verifies a Cognito ID token via aws-jwt-verify (RS256/JWKS,
  iss+aud+exp), then resolves the tenant server-side. DARK BY DEFAULT — rejects
  fast unless COGNITO_AUTH_ENABLED=true AND COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID/COGNITO_CLIENT_ID
  are set, so the MultiAuthGuard falls through to the Firebase/api-key legs
  exactly as today. Additive, behavior-neutral until cutover.
- AuthCognito DAO: resolve-by-sub + link-on-login by VERIFIED email with the
  single-row `ORDER BY id_user ASC LIMIT 1` guard (the exact read-api guard that
  makes the 2 packiot40 dup-email collisions safe). Requires the packiot40
  id_user_cognito column migration.
- Wired into AuthGuardModule + MultiAuthGuard (Cognito added to the OR-set via an
  @Optional() inject so existing 2-arg constructions keep compiling).
- +aws-jwt-verify ^4.0.1.

Tenant is NEVER taken from a token claim: the migrate-on-login Lambda does not
populate custom:id_enterprise, so resolution is DB-only via users.id_user_cognito.

nest build clean; 24 auth tests green (10 new: DAO single-row guard + strategy
dark-by-default + enabled verify/resolve).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
